                            "comparative"
                        ],
                        "form": "more redoubtable"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "86130c1b-5eca-4621-9095-6c36304abe29",
                        "entry_id": "5d3cc0d9-2167-33c8-b52e-9dd26a12367d",
                        "tags": [
                            "superlative"
                        ],
                        "form": "most redoubtable"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "1997d85f-86fe-3f3a-883e-8437437a7787",
                        "entry_id": "5d3cc0d9-2167-33c8-b52e-9dd26a12367d",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Especially of a person.",
                            "Eliciting respect; awe-inspiring, imposing."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "humorous",
                            "sometimes"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "edf5d9e1-ed48-4c65-bca0-7c4f7b90e4a2",
                                "sense_id": "1997d85f-86fe-3f3a-883e-8437437a7787",
                                "text": "The redoubtable New York Times has been called the “newspaper of record” of the United States."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "437d6b11-340d-45c8-8110-2a2fe78bc747",
                                "sense_id": "1997d85f-86fe-3f3a-883e-8437437a7787",
                                "text": "VVhere ſuch an other Rodomont, ſo furious, ſo valorous, ſo redoutable?"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "fe5462d5-ad1d-44b1-8901-e4b27b9bec18",
                                "sense_id": "1997d85f-86fe-3f3a-883e-8437437a7787",
                                "text": "This new batch was sent to Leicester shed, and the redoubtable enginemen who had made such a reputation for themselves with the ex-G.C.R. Atlantics took to the \"B17s\" immediately, although, of course, they required quite different driving methods; […]."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c74fb69c-a336-47c4-b8a4-40c8aa377bcd",
                                "sense_id": "1997d85f-86fe-3f3a-883e-8437437a7787",
                                "text": "Three local yobs have also joined, but they have not reckoned on a redoubtable Conductor and two local revenue protection officers who soon escort them off the train!"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "60231b26-4546-3851-b528-4d9ed2b3fe36",
                        "entry_id": "5d3cc0d9-2167-33c8-b52e-9dd26a12367d",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Especially of a person.",
                            "Eliciting dread or fear; appalling, formidable."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "in a negative sense"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "e0865ba3-21b9-4938-bc30-6819465e0b10",
                                "sense_id": "60231b26-4546-3851-b528-4d9ed2b3fe36",
                                "text": "[I]t pleaſed the grekes at that tyme to ſe yͤ body of Hector ſo trayned by Achilles⸝ bycauſe he was wont to be ſo redoubtab[l]e to them⸝ […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "321bc69a-1521-4f61-ad37-74b1a8c295c8",
                                "sense_id": "60231b26-4546-3851-b528-4d9ed2b3fe36",
                                "text": "Revers'd that ſpear, redoubtable in war, / Reclined that banner, erſt in fields unfurl'd, / That like a deathful meteor, gleam'd afar, / And brav'd the mighty monarchs of the world.— […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5174c600-b735-432a-b1f8-c32bd9687c69",
                                "sense_id": "60231b26-4546-3851-b528-4d9ed2b3fe36",
                                "text": "Inwardly she quaked, because she dreaded and admired the calm, self-contained character of her daughter Winnie, whose displeasure was made redoubtable by a diversity of dreadful silences."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
